  "description": "Define MentorAgent Level-2 specialist agents in YAML instead of C#. Wraps the Agent Framework's declarative agent factory and plugs the resulting agents into MentorAgent's handoff graph, reusing the existing tools with their role checks and human-approval gates intact. Optional — install only if you want file-based agent definitions.",
  "iconFile": "IconMA.png",
  "id": "MentorAgent.Declarative",
  "isPrerelease": true,
  "lastEdited": "2026-08-24T15:33:08.963Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "GdMbsCAqdXPtX+KTvyQOvFdwW0hHlTFa4qUC0m/q1L/7KB0FbEL8PajtvjCo8WX4Yx0u8glMnwTdmWH3JN7ulA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 49663,
  "published": "2026-08-24T15:30:32.507Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-rc.2\n\n\t\tFramework alignment release. No changes to this package's own surface: the YAML dialect, the file scanning rules and the tool-resolution guarantees are exactly as in 1.0.0-rc.1.\n\n\t\t=== Why the version moved ==================================================\n\t\t- The family moves onto the Agent Framework 1.18.0 line; Microsoft.Agents.AI.Declarative moves with it to 1.18.0-rc1, staying on the same line as Microsoft.Agents.AI in the core package rather than drifting onto a different one.\n\n\t\t=== Unchanged, and worth restating ========================================\n\t\t- A tool named in YAML still resolves to a tool the application already registered, already wrapped in MentorAgent's gate, so RequiredRoles and human approval keep working inside a declarative agent's own function-calling loop. A definition file cannot grant itself a capability the application does not already have.\n\t\t- ConfigurationSection still exposes one named section and nothing else. Null means expose nothing, never expose everything.\n\t\t- A definition file is code. Load it only from deploy-time locations.",
